Add --own-numbered=NAME: the client may request and release the bus names
NAME-<digits>[-<digits>...], and nothing else.

A StatusNotifierItem (tray icon) is registered under a well-known name such
as org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-<id> (Chromium/Electron) or
org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-<id> (Qt, libappindicator). --own=NAME.*
only covers dot-separated sub-names (NAME.x), so no existing rule can name
these, short of --own=org.freedesktop.* (far too wide).

Unlike --own, this is not a policy on the names: it only lets RequestName and
ReleaseName through. It gives no SEE or TALK, so the client can neither see
nor call another connection that owns a matching name, and NAME itself,
NAME.x and NAME-<anything but digit groups> stay refused. See the test.

